6. Security & Multi-Tenancy Architecture

Cryptographic Password Storage: Passwords undergo salted PBKDF2 hashing via werkzeug.security. Plaintext passwords are never logged or stored.

Row-Level Tenant Isolation: Every database query filters strictly by user_id = current_user_id parsed from the validated JWT token:

python
Income.query.filter_by(user_id=user_id).all()

Users cannot query, modify, or delete another user's records.

Protection Against SQL Injections: All database operations utilize SQLAlchemy's abstract syntax trees and parameterized bindings.

Session Lifetime & Revocation: JWT access tokens are issued with a 7-day expiration time (JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRES). Expired tokens result in a clean client-side logout and redirect.

